You need to specify a value of F0000000 in R5 at boot time.  Bits 31:28
specify the root directory to boot.  There are a couple of different ways to
accomplish this.  You can deposit a value of F0000000 in R5, then issue the
normal boot command or do something like:

>>>boot <your boot disk> /r5:f0000000.

Do a help at your console to find out the proper syntax for your system.
I'm not sure about a VAX4000, but I believe that the above syntax will
work...

Regards,
Tom

