Get and read the OpenVMS Cluster Systems manual if at all possible.
Yous _SHOULD_ have it if you are managing this configuration.

If you have a cluster of one Alpha and one VAX system you _should_ be able 
to shut down either node and re-boot "standalone" to do the upgrade.  
If a quorum disk is being used correctly for its intended purpose, you 
should not have to adjust quorum.

